  "question": {
    "text": "(a) Baryte, (b) Galena, (c) Zinc blende and (d) Copper pyrites. How many of these minerals are sulphide based?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Baryte is a mineral consisting of barium sulphate&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced></math></p><p>Galena, also called lead glance, is the natural mineral of lead (II) Sulphate&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>PbS</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Zinc blende,&nbsp;is a mineral consisting of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ZnS</mi></math>.</p><p>Copper pyrites is a copper iron sulphide mineral.</p><p>It has the chemical formula&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CuFeS</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>Number of minerals&nbsp;which are sulphide based are 3.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
